  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260914-chern_logconcavity",
  "title": "Binomial log-concavity of the lower-mode forcing term in a rank-two Chern recurrence",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every integer k>=4 define R_k(x)=(x-k+2)A_{k-1,1}(x)+(x-k+3)(x-k+2)A_{k-2,0}(x)/2+(x+1)(x-k+3)A_{k-2,1}(x)+(x+1)(x-k+4)(x-k+3)A_{k-3,0}(x)/2, where A is exactly as defined in source.md and problem.md. If R_k(x)=sum_{r>=0} rho_{k,r} binom(x,r), extended by zero for r<0, then rho_{k,r}>0 exactly for k-2<=r<=2k-1, vanishes otherwise, and rho_{k,r}^2>=rho_{k,r-1}rho_{k,r+1} for every integer r>=0. This is an auxiliary theorem only; neither the j=2 restriction nor the full original Conjecture 3.3 is resolved.",
